X11 apps get the display's fractional scale from the start: xwayland-satellite takes an output's scale from its
mode and xdg-output logical sizes (with fractional scaling), instead of its integer wl_output scale until one of its
windows has been on that output. Until then, X11 apps started first in a session got 200% at 125%. A window's
preferred scale no longer overrides an output's scale from its sizes (a window across two outputs is given one).
For xwayland-satellite v0.8.3 (b83eab9); scripts/build-xwayland-satellite.sh applies it.

